-- dub marimba · wooden tok melody + pluck echo ghost
-- modulation notes:
--   * the dub lives in delayfeedback: 0.75 = dub clouds, 0.85 = runaway, 0.5 = tidy
--   * delaytime (5/12) makes the echoes land off the 4/4 grid — try (7/16) for weirdo
--   * melody is D minor pentatonic over the foundation (Dm7 G7 Cmaj7 Am7):
--     safe notes d5 f5 g5 a5 c6 d6; octave up = thinner, down = moodier
--   * lpf 2500 sweeps closed during breakdowns for underwater marimba
--   * cut 11 = retrigger solo: raise delayfeedback first if you want tails to survive

d11 $ swingBy (1/12) 2 $ cat [
  s "tok" # note "d5 . a5 . ~ . f5 . ~ a5 . d6 . ~ . c6 .",
  s "tok" # note "~ . f5 . a5 . c6 . ~ . a5 . g5 . ~ .",
  s "tok" # note "d5 . g5 . ~ . c6 . ~ a5 . f5 . d5 . ~ .",
  s "tok" # note "a4 . c5 . e5 . g5 . ~ . a5 . ~ . g5 ."
] # gain 0.65 # lpf 2500 # room 0.75 # size 0.9 # delay 0.55 # delaytime (5/12) # delayfeedback 0.75 # cut 11

d14 $ swingBy (1/12) 2 $ struct "t(3,16)" $ s "pluck" # note "<c6 d6 a5 c6>" # gain 0.45 # room 0.6 # delay 0.4 # delaytime (1/3) # delayfeedback 0.7 # cut 14

-- d11 silence
-- d14 silence
